{"description":"Implement steward's single EKA write path: all knowledge/state writes go through the eka-core `api` facade behind one module, carrying correct attribution (`by-kind: worker` where relevant). State the ADR-032 provenance/adopt semantics for every write class (repo-context publish, or workspace-native + explicit adopt), so steward-authored knowledge actually enters a repository snapshot. Steward writes MUST carry deterministic instance-versions (the auto `max+1` publish path is forbidden on the steward write path).","acceptanceCriteria":"All EKA mutations flow through one module; a test proves no other package writes EKA.\nEvery write class states and tests its provenance/adopt semantics (a steward-authored unit is present in the repo snapshot after sync).\nSteward writes carry deterministic instance-versions; a re-issued write is a same-form `PutUnit` no-op (no `max+1` instance).\nWorker processes have no reachable store path (sandbox HOME; `~/.eka` unreadable/unwritable by workers; `eka` authoring verbs absent from worker PATH) - a negative test asserts a worker open of `~/.eka/eka.db` FAILS.\nWrites carry correct attribution. Store integrity holds after a loop run."}